A farmer in Bumthang purchased a tractor of 45 HP at a total cost of Nu 300,000, aiming to operate it for 1,000 hours in a year at an interest rate of 10% after purchase. The life span of the tractor is 10 years and the salvage value is 10% of the initial cost. The housing cost, insurance and taxes were each 1% of the initial cost of the tractor. Fuel consumption of the tractor is 6 litres per hour and it requires a lubricant costing 30% of the fuel cost. In the Bumthang area, the cost of diesel is Nu 24 per litre. The repair and maintenance cost is assumed to be 6% of the initial cost yearly. The machine is operated by an operator paid Nu 150 for 8 hours daily.

Question 2: Describe the maintenance practices required on a tractor before it is put to daily use. (20 marks)', 'Daily (10-hour) checks before work: check engine oil level and top up; check radiator coolant; check fuel and drain water/sediment from the fuel filter; clean the air cleaner (oil-bath or dry element) especially in dusty work; check fan-belt tension; check battery terminals and electrolyte; look for oil, fuel and water leaks; check tyre pressure and wheel nuts; test brakes, clutch free play and steering; grease all grease nipples (front axle, steering, linkages); check lights, horn and hydraulic oil; inspect the three-point hitch, drawbar and PTO guard; warm up the engine and listen for abnormal noise; record the hours in the log book.', null, '[{"point": "Engine oil, coolant/radiator, fuel level and water in fuel", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Air cleaner, fan belt, battery and leaks", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Tyre pressure, wheel nuts, brakes, clutch and steering", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Greasing points, lights, hitch/PTO, log book and warm-up", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
