Question 2: If a driven pulley is made to rotate at 350 rev/min by a driving pulley of 0.3 m diameter running at 1,400 rev/min, determine: (i) the diameter of the driven pulley; (ii) the length of the open belt when the pulleys are 2 m apart; (iii) the length of a cross belt when the pulleys are 2 m apart. (15 marks)', '(i) N₁D₁ = N₂D₂, so D₂ = 0.3 × 1400/350 = 1.2 m.
(ii) Open belt: L = (π/2)(D₁ + D₂) + (D₂ − D₁)²/(4C) + 2C = 1.571 × 1.5 + 0.81/8 + 4 = 2.356 + 0.101 + 4 ≈ 6.46 m.
(iii) Cross belt: L = (π/2)(D₁ + D₂) + (D₁ + D₂)²/(4C) + 2C = 2.356 + 2.25/8 + 4 = 2.356 + 0.281 + 4 ≈ 6.64 m.', null, '[{"point": "(i) D₂ = D₁N₁/N₂ = 0.3 × 1400/350 = 1.2 m", "marks": 5}, {"point": "(ii) L = π(D₁+D₂)/2 + (D₂−D₁)²/4C + 2C = 2.356 + 0.101 + 4 ≈ 6.46 m", "marks": 5}, {"point": "(iii) L = π(D₁+D₂)/2 + (D₁+D₂)²/4C + 2C = 2.356 + 0.281 + 4 ≈ 6.64 m", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
