Question 3: A four-bottom, 40 cm mouldboard plough has a ploughing depth of 17.5 cm and a draft of 1,700 kg. If it is working at a speed of 5.5 km/h and has a field efficiency of 75%, calculate: (i) unit draft; (ii) actual power requirement; (iii) area covered per hour. (15 marks)', '(i) Cross-section = 4 × 40 × 17.5 = 2,800 cm²; unit draft = 1,700/2,800 ≈ 0.61 kg/cm².
(ii) Draft force = 1,700 × 9.81 = 16,677 N; speed = 5.5/3.6 = 1.528 m/s; power = 16,677 × 1.528 ≈ 25,480 W ≈ 25.5 kW (about 34 hp).
(iii) Width = 4 × 0.40 = 1.6 m. Theoretical capacity = 1.6 × 5,500 / 10,000 = 0.88 ha/h; effective = 0.88 × 0.75 = 0.66 ha/h.', null, '[{"point": "(i) Unit draft = 1700/(4 × 40 × 17.5 = 2,800 cm²) ≈ 0.61 kg/cm²", "marks": 5}, {"point": "(ii) P = 1700 × 9.81 × (5.5/3.6) ≈ 25.5 kW (≈ 34 hp)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "(iii) 1.6 m × 5.5 km/h × 0.75 = 0.66 ha/h", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
