Question 4: What are the factors affecting grain storage? What could be some of the probable ideas to improve grain storage in order to help Bhutanese farmers? (10 marks)', 'Factors: moisture content of the grain (above about 12-14% causes moulds and heating), temperature and relative humidity, insects (weevils), rodents and birds, fungi and aflatoxin, the condition of the store (leaks, ventilation), cleanliness and storage time.
Ideas for Bhutan: dry grain properly (solar dryers, tarpaulins) before storage; use hermetic bags and metal or plastic silos instead of open baskets; improve traditional stores with rat guards and sealed floors; community storage and warehouses in each gewog; train farmers in hygiene, safe fumigants and botanical pest control; regular inspection; link to FCB/markets so grain is not stored too long.', null, '[{"point": "Factors: grain moisture, temperature, humidity, insects, rodents, fungi/moulds, storage structure, hygiene", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Ideas: proper drying, hermetic bags/metal bins, improved stores, community storage, training, cold/dry storage, pest management", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
